    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal denotes nonnegative reals; upward arrows are coercions to real numbers. Real.toNNReal(r) is max(r,0) as a nonnegative real. Module.finrank is real vector-space dimension. ContDiff R 2 means C2 regularity. fderiv is the genuine Frechet derivative; gradient is the real inner-product gradient.",
      "A Kernel A B is a measurable family of measures on B indexed by A: for every measurable B-set,its assigned mass is measurable in the index. IsMarkovKernel means every indexed measure is a probability measure. Measure.map means pushforward,Measure.prod is the actual product measure,and Measure.dirac is unit point mass.",
      "ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E is the centered standard Gaussian probability with identity covariance on the finite-dimensional real inner-product space. Smul is real scalar multiplication; Real.sqrt is the nonnegative square root with Mathlib real-domain conventions; real inversion and division are total and give zero when the denominator is zero.",
      "Nested products associate to the right; p.1 and p.2 denote the first and second projections. Nat is the nonnegative integers. A function Nat->E is a sequence. Nat.casesOn n a h equals a if n=0 and h(m) if n=m+1.",
      "Displayed have bindings in the type are local let bindings. Function iteration T^[n] is n-fold composition,including the identity when n=0. Nat.find h is the least natural number satisfying the predicate whose existence is witnessed by h. The dependent if chooses that least number when a witness exists,and zero otherwise.",
      "BorelSpace identifies the measurable structure with the topology. Measurable refers to the full displayed domain,including every product coordinate. Gradients with a fixed parameter p differentiate the state argument,not p. The expanded type is definitionally equal to the compiled theorem type; all local project definition names have been removed. This supplies only library definitions,no source identity or extra conclusions."
    ]
